From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:10:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: the validator counts a misaligned exclusive
 access apart instead of calling it a difference (#15)

The five cases left on Xenoblade 2 sdk are Unicorn stopping on ldxr, ldxrh,
ldaxr or ldaxrh at an odd address. ARM faults on an exclusive access that is
not aligned to its size and x86 does not, so the recompiled code goes on.
misaligned_exclusive() checks the instruction (an exclusive load or store,
never a byte one) and the real value of its base register at the stop, and
only then is the case counted in its own column. An unaligned ordinary
load, any other instruction and an address outside the image are still
differences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Unicorn faults on a misaligned exclusive access and x86 does not: counted apart, only when verified
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#15

---
